            "pdfPage": 17,
            "printedPage": 9
          }
        ],
        "text": "(Several women inside are busy with wedding preparations. Kumudha arrives. Poomalai eagerly runs to her—)",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s007-u002",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பூமாலை",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s007-d001",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 17,
            "printedPage": 9
          }
        ],
        "text": "Kumudha!",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s007-u003",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "குமுதா",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s007-d002",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 17,
            "printedPage": 9
          }
        ],
        "text": "Chinnamma! (They embrace.)",
        "notes": [
          "The kinship address `சின்னம்மா` is transliterated rather than assigned a narrower English relationship."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s007-u004",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பூமாலை",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s007-d003",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 17,
            "printedPage": 9
          }
        ],
        "text": "Why are you so late, dear?",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s007-u005",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "குமுதா",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s007-d004",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 17,
            "printedPage": 9
          }
        ],
        "text": "Exams, Chinnamma. I couldn't come at once...",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s007-u006",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பூமாலை",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s007-d005",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 17,
            "printedPage": 9
          }
        ],
        "text": "Sit down, Kumudha. I had thought I would marry you to my younger brother and keep you here in the household...",
        "notes": [
          "The corrected source's `வீட்டோட இருப்பேன்னு` is retained; the historical English had dropped the household-continuity phrase."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s007-u007",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "குண்டுமணி",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s007-d006",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 17,
            "printedPage": 9
          }
        ],
        "text": "But before that, he already went and had a love marriage.",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s007-u008",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "குமுதா",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s007-d007",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 17,
            "printedPage": 9
          }
        ],
        "text": "Hey, Gundumani.",
        "notes": [
          "The corrected source label is `குண்டுமணி`; the stale `குணமணி` metadata is not retained."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s007-u009",
        "kind": "stage-direction",
        "speakerLabel": null,
        "sourceRecordId": null,
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 17,
            "printedPage": 9
          }
        ],
        "text": "(Paranthaman enters.)",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s007-u010",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பரந்தாமன்",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s007-d008",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 17,
            "printedPage": 9
          }
        ],
        "text": "Ah! When did Goddess Kumudha arrive?",
        "notes": [
          "The mock-formal `தேவி` is retained as `Goddess` to preserve Paranthaman's playful register."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s007-u011",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "குமுதா",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s007-d009",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 17,
            "printedPage": 9
          }
        ],
        "text": "Uncle, you're still in full bridegroom style! Tell me, is my aunt fair or dark?",
        "notes": [
          "`மாப்பிள்ளை முறுக்கிலேயே` is retained as a joking reference to his bridegroom swagger/style, not location."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s007-u012",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "பரந்தாமன்",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s007-d010",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 17,
            "printedPage": 9
          }
        ],
        "text": "Oh dear...and an educated girl doesn't even know this! Would anyone like a woman if she were red in colour? Blood and kumkum are red—who would touch that colour? From now on, ask like this: lemon-fruit colour, jamun-fruit colour, or a mixture of the two?",
        "notes": [
          "The source's colour-based joking and period vocabulary are translated without modernization."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s007-u013",
        "kind": "stage-direction",
        "speakerLabel": null,
        "sourceRecordId": null,
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 17,
            "printedPage": 9
          }
        ],
        "text": "(Kumudha laughs.)",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s007-u014",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "குமுதா",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s007-d011",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 18,
            "printedPage": 10
          }
        ],
        "text": "In the excitement of the wedding, poetry is pouring out of Uncle!",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s007-u015",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "குண்டுமணி",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s007-d012",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 18,
            "printedPage": 10
          }
        ],
        "text": "And colour poetry is pouring out too! (Laughter)",
        "notes": [
          "The corrected source reads `கலர் கவிதைகளால்ல`; the historical `cover-poetry` rendering was based on stale text."
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
